  },
  "holistic_F_N": 3,
  "holistic_F_H": -3,
  "section_notes": "The final rules are largely safety-oriented, but S2 is weakened because exceeding the 5% test-failure threshold triggers corrective action rather than a sales stop. S5 imposes a mandatory model-specific recall above 8/100k after regulator verification, which would likely hit Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9/100k). Northwind's red lines are met: no public per-model rates, and the 72-month retrofit deadline meets its 6-year minimum."
 },
